From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] boards/rpi_4b: add Zephyr Dom0 board conf + overlay (BCM2711)

Add the Raspberry Pi 4 (BCM2711) counterpart of boards/rpi_5.{conf,overlay}.
Both are new files, so this patch adds nothing to the RPi5 board and the two can
coexist in one checkout.

The Zephyr-side fixes that patch 0008 root-caused on RPi5 hardware are folded
into rpi_4b.conf rather than re-derived: the raised shell/main/ISR stacks plus
HW_STACK_PROTECTION, MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32, LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE, the 0x18 domctl
interface version with XENTROOPS_ARCH_* = n, and DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n with
FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT=4 for an SD-less Dom0. None of them is BCM2712
specific.

Three things are genuinely different on BCM2711 and are commented in place:

* CELLS. This overlay keeps the root at 1/1 and writes single-cell addresses
  because everything it needs is below 4 GiB (Dom0 bank at 0x20000000, grant table
  at 0x02000000). That is a choice, not a constraint: /soc gets its own
  #address-cells = <1> / #size-cells = <1> from dts/arm64/armv8-a.dtsi
  independently of the root, so raising the root to <2> as rpi_5.overlay does would
  not disturb its children. (An earlier revision of this paragraph claimed
  bcm2711.dtsi gives /soc no cells and that /soc's children therefore depend on the
  root -- the opposite of what the overlay body says, and wrong.)

* CONSOLE. rpi_4b.dts points zephyr,console at &uart1, the BCM2711 aux/mini
  UART. Xen owns the console (boot.cmd passes dtuart=/soc/serial@7e201000, the
  pl011) and Xen's rpi4 platform blacklists the aux peripheral's page
  neighbours, so Dom0 uses the Xen PV console and &uart1 is disabled. The pinned
  Zephyr rev does define pl011 nodes for BCM2711 (uart0 at 0xfe201000, which is the
  very UART Xen takes, plus uart2..uart5), but they are all status = "disabled"
  there and none is enabled here.

* SRAM RELINK to 0x20000000, derived rather than measured. Xen's rpi4 platform
  sets .dma_bitsize = 30, so allocate_memory_11() confines Dom0's bank[0] to
  below 1 GiB -- RPi5 has no platform entry, gets the 32-bit default and landed
  at 0xc0000000. boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in passes dom0_mem=128M
  (get_allocation_size(128 MiB) is exactly order 15), and the first free
  naturally-aligned 128 MiB block below 1 GiB in that memory map is
  0x20000000-0x28000000. (dom0_mem used to be 256M; the overlay body records why
  that could never be satisfied as one block on this board. An earlier revision of
  this paragraph still derived the address from 256M / order 16.)

  There is NO automatic guard on this value. tools/check-memory-map.py models
  BCM2712 only -- meta-xt-rpi4/README.md says so, and its ZEPHYR_SRAM_PATCH is
  hardcoded to 0008-rpi5-board-domd-owns-sd.patch -- so a drift here is silent.
  Read BANK[0] off the Xen console on the first boot; a mismatch is total UART
  silence with no Dom0 console at all.

The hypervisor node's grant-table base is likewise derived (find_gnttab_region()
uses __pa(_stext), i.e. boot.cmd's 0x02000000 Xen load address); its size and the
extended region still have to be confirmed against the first boot's Xen log, and
the exact log lines to read are quoted in the overlay.

Rebased onto Zephyr 4.4.1 (the pins moved in 0021; the west manifest is shared by
every board, so rpi_4b moves with rpi_5):
 - CONFIG_FS_MULTI_PARTITION -> CONFIG_FS_FATFS_MULTI_PARTITION, and the two
   CONFIG_XEN_DOMCTL_XENTROOPS_ARCH_* lines are dropped. All three were hard
   Kconfig errors on 4.x: the first is spelled differently upstream, the other two
   existed only in the xen-troops Zephyr fork.
 - CONFIG_HW_STACK_PROTECTION=y is dropped and CONFIG_STACK_SENTINEL=y takes its
   place. Only CPU_AARCH64_CORTEX_R selects ARCH_HAS_STACK_PROTECTION on arm64, so
   the assignment was invisible and never reached .config - the comment that said so
   was right, but the substitute it claimed did not exist does.
 - the logical drive moves from "1" to "0" and an inert ramdisk0 is declared:
   4.4.1 derives FF_VOLUMES from the status-okay devicetree disk nodes, and rpi_4b
   had none, which fails to compile ff.c and fails the BUILD_ASSERT(FF_VOLUMES == 1)
   that 0028 adds to the shared src/storage.c.
 - CONFIG_DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n and the FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT pin are dropped:
   the symbol is invisible without an SDHC node, and 0026 fixes the Kconfig default
   the pin was working around.
 - CONFIG_XEN_SYSCTL_INTERFACE_VERSION=0x16, CONFIG_XEN_REGIONS=y and
   CONFIG_XENSTORE_TREE_TRAVERSE_DEPTH=16 are added, matching rpi_5.conf: 0022
   widens the sysctl range, 0023 backports the extended-regions driver (opt-in
   upstream, where the fork defaulted it on) and 0031 needs the depth bound.
 - the chosen zephyr,entropy property, the gpio-leds node and its led0 alias are
   deleted, and gpio1 disabled - the same dangling-phandle class of failure that
   CONFIG_PCIE=n works around for rpi_5.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-dom0-xt]
---
diff --git a/boards/rpi_4b.conf b/boards/rpi_4b.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..de2a59d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/rpi_4b.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Copyright (c) 2026 Yuichi Kusakabe
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#
+# Zephyr Dom0 configuration for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (BCM2711).
+#
+# Derived from boards/rpi_5.conf with patch 0008's hardware-verified fixes folded
+# in, because they were all root-caused on the Zephyr side and are not BCM2712
+# specific:
+#   - the raised shell/main/ISR stacks (xu create's domain build has large VLAs
+#     and overflowed a 4 KiB shell stack) plus STACK_SENTINEL, which is the only
+#     overflow detection available on Cortex-A,
+#   - MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32 (arch/arm64/core/Kconfig:335 defaults to 8 for this board
+#     -- no USERSPACE and ARM64_VA_BITS=36 < 40, so neither the 12/16/20 branch
+#     applies -- and mapping a multi-MiB guest kernel exhausts 8),
+#   - LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE (async logging interleaved with the shell on the shared
+#     Xen console made failure lines unreadable),
+#   - the 0x18 domctl interface version for Xen 4.22,
+#   - the SD-less Dom0 handling.
+#
+# Written for Zephyr 4.4.1. The 3.6-era spellings this file used to carry are gone:
+# FS_MULTI_PARTITION is FS_FATFS_MULTI_PARTITION upstream, and
+# XEN_DOMCTL_XENTROOPS_ARCH_{VGSX_OSID,SCI_TYPE} existed only in the xen-troops
+# Zephyr fork -- on 4.x an assignment to an undefined symbol is a hard Kconfig
+# error, so all three would fail the build outright.
+#
+# RPi4-specific notes are marked [rpi4].
+
+CONFIG_XEN_DOM0=y
+
+CONFIG_XSTAT=y
+CONFIG_XSTAT_SHELL_CMDS=y
+
+# xu create runs on the shell thread and its domain build (load_modules ->
+# gen_domain_fdt) has large VLAs; 4 KiB overflowed and corrupted adjacent
+# .data/.bss on RPi5. Overflow detection comes from CONFIG_STACK_SENTINEL below;
+# HW stack protection is not available on this platform.
+CONFIG_SHELL_STACK_SIZE=32768
+
+CONFIG_MAIN_STACK_SIZE=16384
+CONFIG_ISR_STACK_SIZE=16384
+# CONFIG_HW_STACK_PROTECTION is deliberately NOT set: on arm64 only
+# CPU_AARCH64_CORTEX_R selects ARCH_HAS_STACK_PROTECTION (arch/arm64/core/Kconfig),
+# so on this Cortex-A72 the symbol is invisible and the assignment never reached
+# .config. Kconfig does not error on assignments to *invisible* symbols (only
+# undefined ones), which is why an earlier revision of this file could carry it
+# for so long without anyone noticing.
+#
+# CONFIG_STACK_SENTINEL is the substitute that does work here (subsys/debug/Kconfig;
+# MULTITHREADING=y, !USERSPACE, and MPU_STACK_GUARD is arm32-only, so all its
+# dependencies are met). It writes a magic word at the low end of every stack and
+# checks it on context switch, on an interrupt that does not switch, on thread exit
+# and on k_yield(), turning an overflow into a reported thread kill instead of
+# silent corruption of whatever follows in RAM. That matters most for the recursive
+# xenstore teardown paths bounded by patch 0031.
+CONFIG_STACK_SENTINEL=y
+CONFIG_MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32
+
+CONFIG_XEN_VCH=y
+CONFIG_XEN_DOM0LESS_BOOT=y
+
+CONFIG_USE_DEFAULT_DOM_CFG=n
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_BUILTIN_IMAGES=n
+
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_ENABLE=y
+
+CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_SHELL=y
+
+CONFIG_NOCACHE_MEMORY=y
+# FS_FATFS_MULTI_PARTITION, not the fork's FS_MULTI_PARTITION (upstream spelling,
+# subsys/fs/Kconfig.fatfs).
+CONFIG_FS_FATFS_MULTI_PARTITION=y
+# Volume "0:", not "1:". On Zephyr 4.4 FF_VOLUMES is derived from the number of
+# status-okay devicetree disk nodes, and rpi_4b.overlay declares exactly one (the
+# inert ramdisk0 it adds so FatFs compiles at all), so "1:" is out of range.
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_LOGICAL_DRIVE_NAME="0"
+# Guest images live in the FAT root of SD p1, not in a dom0/ subdirectory
+# (same as the RPi5 SoDeV build; patch 0002 makes that change for rpi_5.conf).
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_DIR=""
+CONFIG_XEN_LIBFDT=y
+
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_LINUX_PV_DOMAIN=y
+
+CONFIG_XRUN_STORAGE_DMA_DEBOUNCE=4
+
+CONFIG_DOMU_MAX=5
+
+# Synchronous logging so a `xu create` failure line prints atomically on the
+# shared Xen console.
+CONFIG_LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE=y
+
+# [rpi4] SD-less Dom0. boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in marks
+# /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000 xen,passthrough, so the SD controller belongs to DomD
+# (which owns the toolstack and serves the guest rootfs partitions over
+# virtio-blk). With its MMIO unmapped, an enabled SDHC controller would hang the
+# driver's SYS_INIT on the first register access and stop the init chain BEFORE
+# dom0less_init, so the dom0less DomD would never be introduced to xenstore.
+# rpi_4b.overlay therefore does not enable any SDHC node.
+#
+# Neither CONFIG_DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n nor a FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT pin is set:
+# with no SDHC node upstream 4.4.1 leaves DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC invisible (assigning to
+# it risks a Kconfig warning, which 4.x turns into a build error), and patch 0026
+# fixes zephyr-dom0-xt/Kconfig to read `default SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT if SDHC` /
+# `default 4`, so the empty, invisible SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT can no longer leak
+# into the generated misc/generated/configs.c assembly.
+
+# Xen 4.21 ABI. XEN_DOMCTL_XENTROOPS_ARCH_{VGSX_OSID,SCI_TYPE} used to be set to n
+# here to keep arm_sci_type/vgsx_osid out of xen_arch_domainconfig; those symbols
+# exist only in the xen-troops Zephyr fork and are absent from 4.4.1, where patch
+# 0024 removes the vendored public headers entirely and the ABI comes from
+# zephyr-xenlib's copy of Xen 4.21.0's.
+CONFIG_XEN_DOMCTL_INTERFACE_VERSION=0x18
+# Xen 4.21's sysctl.h declares 0x16. Patch 0022 widens the Kconfig range that far;
+# at 0x15 `xu list` and `xstat physinfo` print nothing at all, silently.
+CONFIG_XEN_SYSCTL_INTERFACE_VERSION=0x16
+
+# Extended regions (patch 0023 backports the upstream driver). Without this xenlib
+# carves the guest-image mapping window out of Dom0's own 2 MiB heap, which a
+# multi-MiB guest kernel does not fit.
+CONFIG_XEN_REGIONS=y
+
+# Deepest path this system writes is 8 components
+# (.../backend/vbd/<fe>/<devid>/multi-queue-max-queues), and the PV protocol headers
+# document 8 too; pvUSB reaches 9 and pvSCSI 10. Patch 0031 bounds tree depth at
+# creation time with this symbol to keep the recursive free off the end of the
+# xenstore worker stack, so leaving it at the default 8 would sit exactly at the
+# limit. Use the Kconfig maximum; 0031 sized the worker stack (8 KiB) for it.
+CONFIG_XENSTORE_TREE_TRAVERSE_DEPTH=16
+
+# SoDeV production guests (see src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c). Also settable from the
+# moulin builder vars in rpi4-sodev.yaml.
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_SODEV=y
diff --git a/boards/rpi_4b.overlay b/boards/rpi_4b.overlay
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..494f965
--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/rpi_4b.overlay
@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 Yuichi Kusakabe
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+ *
+ * Zephyr Dom0 device-tree overlay for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (BCM2711).
+ *
+ * Counterpart of boards/rpi_5.overlay. Three BCM2711 differences shape it:
+ *
+ *  1. CELLS. This overlay keeps the root at #address-cells = <1> /
+ *     #size-cells = <1> because every address it needs is below 4 GiB: the Dom0
+ *     bank is at 0x20000000 and the grant table at 0x02000000. That is a choice,
+ *     NOT a constraint — /soc gets its own #address-cells = <1> / #size-cells =
+ *     <1> from dts/arm64/armv8-a.dtsi:10-15, independently of the root, so its
+ *     children are unaffected by the root's cells and the root could be raised to
+ *     <2> exactly as rpi_5.overlay does (rpi_5.overlay:26-28) if a >4 GiB address
+ *     were ever needed here.
+ *
+ *  2. CONSOLE. rpi_4b.dts points zephyr,console at &uart1, the BCM2711 aux/mini
+ *     UART. Under Xen that UART is not Dom0's to use: Xen owns the console
+ *     (boot.cmd passes console=dtuart dtuart=/soc/serial@7e201000, the pl011) and
+ *     the aux peripheral's page neighbours are on Xen's rpi4 device blacklist.
+ *     Dom0 therefore talks over the Xen PV console, exactly as on RPi5, and the
+ *     board's UART is disabled. NOTE: bcm2711.dtsi DOES define pl011 nodes (uart0
+ *     at 0xfe201000 is the one Xen takes, plus uart2..uart5), but they ship
+ *     status = "disabled" and none is enabled here.
+ *
+ *  3. NO SDHC. The RPi4 SD controller (/emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000) is handed to DomD
+ *     by boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in, and the pinned rpi_4b board does not define
+ *     an SDHC node at all — so unlike rpi_5.overlay there is nothing to disable
+ *     here. boards/rpi_4b.conf still sets CONFIG_DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n so the disk
+ *     driver is not built.
+ */
+
+/delete-node/ &sram0;
+
+#include <mem.h>
+
+/ {
+	chosen {
+		zephyr,console = &xen_consoleio_hvc;
+		zephyr,shell-uart = &xen_consoleio_hvc;
+		/*
+		 * rpi_4b.dts points zephyr,entropy at &rng. Delete the property rather
+		 * than merely disabling the node: gen_defines resolves a chosen phandle
+		 * regardless of status, so the first subsystem to select
+		 * CONFIG_ENTROPY_GENERATOR would expand DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_CHOSEN(...)) to
+		 * a __device_dts_ord_N that was never emitted -- an undeclared-identifier
+		 * error. rpi_5 needed CONFIG_PCIE=n for exactly this reason.
+		 */
+		/delete-property/ zephyr,entropy;
+	};
+
+	psci {
+		method = "hvc";
+	};
+
+	xen_consoleio_hvc: hvc {
+		compatible = "xen,hvc-consoleio";
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * reg[0] = grant table, reg[1..N] = extended regions.
+	 *
+	 * Xen writes the real values into the domain device tree, but Zephyr
+	 * cannot parse them at runtime, so they are hard-coded here and MUST be
+	 * confirmed against the first boot's Xen log:
+	 *   (XEN) Grant table range: 0x............-0x............
+	 *   (XEN) d0: extended region 1: 0x..........->0x..........
+	 *
+	 * Derivation of the values below (see also
+	 * rpi4-port/meta-rpi5-sodev/meta-xt-common/meta-xt-dom0-zephyr/RPI4-PORT.md):
+	 *
+	 *   grant table: find_gnttab_region() in xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c sets
+	 *     gnttab_start = __pa(_stext), i.e. where boot.cmd loaded the Xen binary
+	 *     -> 0x02000000, and gnttab_size = gnttab_dom0_frames() << PAGE_SHIFT
+	 *     = min(gnttab_max_frames, PFN_DOWN(_etext - _stext)) frames. MEASURED
+	 *     from this build's xen-syms map: _stext 0xa0000200000, _etext
+	 *     0xa0000277978 -> 0x77978 = 0.47 MiB = 119 frames, so the real region is
+	 *     0x77000 (rpi_5 measured 0x7b000). 0x100000 over-declares ~2x, which is
+	 *     harmless; under-declaring is not. Earlier text here guessed "about 1 MiB".
+	 *
+	 *   extended region 1: find_unallocated_memory()
+	 *     (xen/common/device-tree/domain-build.c) does NOT report holes in the
+	 *     memory map. It seeds a rangeset from bootinfo_get_mem() — the RAM banks
+	 *     only — and then subtracts the assigned ones, so a physical range that is
+	 *     not RAM can never come out of it. The gpu_mem carve-out is exactly that,
+	 *     which is why this used to name 0x3b400000-0x40000000 and was wrong. The
+	 *     value below mirrors rpi_5.overlay's measured shape: the unallocated RAM
+	 *     above Xen and below DomD's lowest static-mem bank. Confirm from the log.
+	 */
+	hypervisor: hypervisor@2000000 {
+		compatible = "xen,xen";
+		reg = <0x02000000 0x100000>, <0x02200000 0x05e00000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 0x0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE IRQ_DEFAULT_PRIORITY>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Dom0's direct-map RAM bank. Xen loads the Dom0 image at
+	 * bank[0].start + text_offset and cannot be told where to put it
+	 * (construct_hwdom -> allocate_memory_11 ignores xen,static-mem, which is a
+	 * dom0less-domU-only mechanism), while Zephyr is absolute-linked from
+	 * CONFIG_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS, auto-derived from this node. A mismatch runs
+	 * garbage and faults before console init — on RPi5 the symptom was total UART
+	 * silence and no xu-create.
+	 *
+	 * 0x20000000 is derived, not copied from RPi5 (which uses 0xc0000000):
+	 *   - Xen's rpi4 platform sets .dma_bitsize = 30
+	 *     (xen/arch/arm/platforms/brcm-raspberry-pi.c), so allocate_memory_11()
+	 *     computes lowmem_bitsize = min(32, 30) = 30 and confines bank[0] to
+	 *     below 1 GiB. RPi5 has no platform entry, gets the 32-bit default, and
+	 *     therefore landed at 0xc0000000.
+	 *   - boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in passes dom0_mem=128M, and
+	 *     get_allocation_size(128 MiB) is exactly order 15 = 128 MiB.
+	 *   - In that boot script's memory map the first free naturally-aligned
+	 *     128 MiB block below 1 GiB is 0x20000000: everything under it is taken
+	 *     (boot modules below 0x08000000, DomD static-mem bank1
+	 *     0x08000000-0x20000000), and the map deliberately leaves this hole.
+	 * NOTE: nothing checks this automatically. tools/check-memory-map.py models
+	 * BCM2712 only (meta-xt-rpi4/README.md; its ZEPHYR_SRAM_PATCH is hardcoded to
+	 * the rpi5 patch), so a drift here is silent. Confirm BANK[0] from the Xen
+	 * console on the first boot -- the CONFIRM block below is that check.
+	 *
+	 * SIZE IS 128 MiB, NOT 256 (changed 2026-08-04). dom0_mem used to be 256M,
+	 * but 256 MiB could never be satisfied as one block on this board: the
+	 * firmware places the host DT blob at 0x2eff1f00 (observed on hardware as
+	 * MODULE[1] 0x2eff1f00-0x2f000fff), which is inside 0x20000000-0x30000000,
+	 * so allocate_memory_11() halved the order and Dom0 actually received
+	 * 128 MiB @0x20000000 + 128 MiB @0x30000000 -- two banks with a hole between
+	 * them, while this node claimed one contiguous 256 MiB region. Zephyr would
+	 * have treated 0x28000000-0x30000000 as its own RAM and faulted on use.
+	 * Asking for 128M makes the request equal to the first bank, so the
+	 * declaration matches what Xen hands over, and it returns 128 MiB to the
+	 * guest budget -- which is what makes the 4 GiB three-domain cockpit fit.
+	 * Do NOT lower it further: the scan starts at address 0, so 64M matches
+	 * 0x04000000 and 32M matches 0x00000000, where config.txt's
+	 * armstub=bl31.bin (TF-A BL31 + the secondary-CPU spin tables) lives.
+	 *
+	 * CONFIRM on the first boot:
+	 *   (XEN) Allocating 1:1 mappings totalling 128MB for dom0:
+	 *   (XEN) BANK[0] 0x000020000000-0x000028000000 (128MB)
+	 *   (XEN) Loading zImage from 0x02400000 to 0x20000000-0x2.......
+	 */
+	sram0: memory@20000000 {
+		compatible = "mmio-sram";
+		reg = <0x20000000 DT_SIZE_M(128)>;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * rpi_4b.dts declares a gpio-leds node whose led_act child drives &gpio1. Dom0
+	 * does not own that GPIO block, and a node referencing a disabled controller is
+	 * the same dangling-phandle hazard as the chosen property above, so the node and
+	 * the alias that names it both go. The alias has to go FIRST - a dangling alias
+	 * is a devicetree error ("/aliases: undefined node label 'led_act'").
+	 *
+	 * By node name, not by label: rpi_4b.dts spells it `leds {`, with no label, so
+	 * `/delete-node/ &leds;` would not resolve.
+	 */
+	aliases {
+		/delete-property/ led0;
+	};
+	/delete-node/ leds;
+
+	/*
+	 * Zephyr 4.x derives FatFs's FF_VOLUMES from the devicetree instead of letting
+	 * a board hardcode it: FF_VOLUME_STRS is the disk-name of every status-okay disk
+	 * node. rpi_4b has none, which leaves FF_VOLUMES at 0 -- the generated
+	 * zephyr_fatfs_config.h then undefines FF_VOLUME_STRS while ff.c still
+	 * references VolumeStr[] under FF_STR_VOLUME_ID == 1, so the build fails. It
+	 * would also fail the BUILD_ASSERT(FF_VOLUMES == 1) that patch 0028 adds to the
+	 * shared src/storage.c.
+	 *
+	 * So declare one deliberately tiny RAM disk, exactly as rpi_5.overlay does. It
+	 * is never mounted: storage_init() fails earlier, at disk_access_init("SD") with
+	 * -ENODEV, because the SD controller is DomD's. 4 KiB is the cost of keeping the
+	 * storage code compiling.
+	 */
+	ramdisk0: ramdisk0 {
+		compatible = "zephyr,ram-disk";
+		disk-name = "RAM";
+		sector-size = <512>;
+		sector-count = <8>;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * Dom0 has no GPIO here, and gpio1 is the controller the deleted leds node
+ * referenced. Harmless only while CONFIG_GPIO is off, and that is one
+ * `select GPIO` away.
+ */
+&gpio1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
+ * Same reasoning for the RNG, and deleting the chosen zephyr,entropy property is
+ * NOT enough on its own: drivers/entropy/Kconfig.iproc has
+ * `default y` under `depends on DT_HAS_BRCM_IPROC_RNG200_ENABLED`, and leaving the
+ * node status = "okay" sets that symbol. The moment anything selects
+ * CONFIG_ENTROPY_GENERATOR the driver builds and its init touches 0xfe104000, MMIO
+ * this Dom0 does not own -- the failure 0008 documents for the RPi5 SDHCI node,
+ * where SYS_INIT hangs before dom0less_init and DomD is never introduced to
+ * xenstore. rpi_5.overlay disables &rng for exactly this reason.
+ */
+&rng {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The BCM2711 aux/mini UART: Xen owns the console, Dom0 uses the PV console.
+ * Disabling it also keeps Dom0 away from the aux peripheral page that Xen's rpi4
+ * blacklist protects (brcm,bcm2835-aux / -aux-spi).
+ */
+&uart1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
